{"chunk_id": "68f817fc33bf", "text": "Arjuna encounters a mysterious hunter (Kirata) in the Himalayas who calmly withstands the storm of arrows shot from the Gandiva. Confident that no being except Rudra could endure such force, Arjuna continues the fight even after his arrows are exhausted, attacking with bow, sword, rocks, trees, and finally his bare fists. The hunter effortlessly breaks his weapons and overpowers him in brutal hand\u2011to\u2011hand combat, leaving Arjuna nearly dead. Regaining consciousness, Arjuna fashions a clay image of Shiva and offers a garland in devotion\u2014only to see the same garland appear on the Kirata\u2019s head. Realizing the truth, he bows. Shiva reveals himself, praises Arjuna\u2019s courage and austerities, forgives him, and promises to grant him a mighty, irresistible weapon.\nArjuna battles a mysterious Kirata\u2014actually Shiva\u2014until defeated, then realizes the truth and worships him, earning Shiva\u2019s favor and promise of a divine weapon.\nThemes: divine test, humility after defeat, Shiva\u2019s revelation, heroic endurance, granting of celestial weapon", "vector": [-0.0033490038476884365, -0.013268113136291504, -0.015173174440860748, 0.03618943691253662, 0.005610843654721975, 0.025782279670238495, -0.03007708303630352, -0.014917371794581413, -0.023816633969545364, -0.01995265670120716, 0.009444527328014374, 0.00504201790317893, -0.002527740551158786, -0.005388698540627956, 0.005657965317368507, 0.003216053359210491, 0.04661005362868309, -0.01870056800544262, 0.02374931611120701, -0.019710317254066467, -0.01913139410316944, 0.020504653453826904, -0.014701957814395428, 0.011517880484461784, -0.012924798764288425, 0.015846341848373413, 0.012480508536100388, -0.029996301978826523, 0.0076539041474461555, -0.01110724825412035, -0.008508825674653053, 0.001101468806155026, -0.005392064340412617, -0.003039347007870674, -0.02759983018040657, 0.0012217973126098514, -0.0016644044080749154, -0.016209851950407028, 0.0049040187